course: dictionary
lesson: 13993
title: A word that can hurt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Loony» is an informal word. It means crazy or very silly, and people often use it to tease. Look at the clues around it: «Her plan to swim across the lake in winter was a loony idea.» The idea was dangerous and silly, so loony must mean silly or crazy.
explain: Be careful with this word. «Loony» can be rude and hurtful, especially when it is used about a person. Some people with illnesses in their minds are upset by it. In your own writing, use a kinder word such as silly, odd or surprising.
explain: The same spelling can mean something else in Canada. Spelt «loonie», it is the one-dollar coin, and it has a loon bird on it. «Sam paid for the juice with one loonie.» Here, the context tells you it is money, not a silly person.
fact: «Loony» is an informal word, so it is for chatting, not for formal writing.
fact: As a noun, «a loony» means a crazy or very silly person.
fact: As an adjective, «loony» means crazy or silly, as in «a loony idea».
fact: In Canada, spelt «loonie», it means the one-dollar coin with a loon bird on it.
fact: «Loony» can be hurtful, so choose kinder words like silly or surprising when you write.
exercise: «Her plan to swim across the lake in winter was a loony idea.» What does loony mean here? | Wise and careful | *Crazy or very silly | Very quick | Wet and cold
exercise: In Canada, Sam pays with a loonie. How much money is one loonie? | Ten dollars | Fifty cents | Five dollars | *One dollar
exercise: «The loon swam calmly on the lake.» Copy the word that names the bird. | calmly | lake | swam | *loon
test: Why should you be careful when you use the word loony? | It is a formal word used in school reports | *It is informal and can hurt people, so choose a kinder word | It means the same as happy | It only means one dollar everywhere
test: In Canada, what is a loonie? | A petrol station | A loon bird that lives in a park | *A one-dollar coin with a loon on it | A kind of hat
exam: What does loony mean in «Tom's idea to ride a bike along the roof was loony»? | *Crazy or very silly | Lost on the way home | Very quiet | Happy and calm
